taskPackages.summary:
Implement the complete AlembicCore producer foundation for the confirmed Recipe production/retrieval-quality requirement, starting from clean baseline d17db939ed49ea30bdbf380f400b783530b6d6a8 and returning one clean Core commit.

Required connected implementation:
1. Add the additive, Recipe-embedded retrieval profile contract across KnowledgeEntry/domain, Markdown serialization, SQLite/API wire and public exports. Preserve old Recipes through a versioned compatibility projector; do not add a separate retrieval database or state machine. Profile semantics must include schema version, project-primary summary, evidence-grounded technical English summary/concepts/scenarios/exclusions, field/source provenance and deterministic content hashes.
2. Implement deterministic RetrievalReadiness and connect it to the real Recipe production/persistence/publish path, not an unused facade. pending/staging may retain repairable violations; every active transition uses the same readiness result. Provider availability, vector state, query ranks and frozen acceptance queries must be absent from hard readiness inputs. Include at least one real in-test production consumer through persistence and projection.
3. Replace conflicting sparse/dense Recipe material with one RecipeRetrievalDocumentSet projector: required intent plus information-dense, non-duplicate optional guidance/implementation/rationale roles. Raw paths, evidence IDs, quality bookkeeping and bridge metadata are provenance only. Sparse and dense serialize/weight the same facts and hashes. Retire fixed nine-region active Recipe candidate generation and prevent generic entry vectors from competing as a second Recipe representation, while preserving accepted KnowledgeRetrievalPort, truth projection, refill, raw lane evidence and query-side reader-only boundaries.
4. Make lifecycle derivation identical for knowledge events, incremental maintenance and full build. Add generation manifest identity covering projection schema/provider/model/dimension/format/corpus; exact per-Recipe expected IDs; detection/repair planning for orphan, missing, partial, duplicate, hash mismatch and stale generation; provider-independent delete/deprecate cleanup; verified replacement; shadow build, atomic active switch and rollback. A failed build must leave the old generation queryable. No query-time projector persistence, reconcile, rebuild or writer construction.
5. Preserve compatibility for existing Core and outer consumers through stable package exports and explicit diagnostics. Exact TypeScript shape may adapt only within confirmed semantics.

Required RED/GREEN evidence:
- profile Markdown/domain/SQLite/API round-trip without field loss;
- ungrounded/default/whole-file code evidence produces stable readiness violations and cannot publish active;
- provider offline yields the same readiness decision;
- compatibility projection never invents English facts;
- projector emits required/distinct roles and sparse+dense share source/profile/document hashes;
- incremental and full derivation are byte-equivalent for the same Recipe;
- same-dimension model or projection-schema changes require a new generation;
- exact reconcile catches orphan/missing/partial/duplicate/stale-generation fixtures;
- update verifies full replacement before old removal; delete works without provider;
- failed shadow build preserves active generation and rollback restores it;
- public Search/Prime/Recipe retrieval call graphs remain reader-only and existing truth/refill tests pass.

Repository gates and return:
- run focused tests, npm run test, npm run build:check, npm run build, npm run lint and npm run check as applicable under repository rules, plus Core delivery/tool/Codex/package boundary tests;
- review git diff/check, public exports, migrations and compatibility;
- two-stage self-review: requirement compliance, then correctness/failure paths/performance/maintainability;
- commit only AlembicCore, return exact parent/commit, changed files/symbols, raw command summaries, compatibility notes and residual risks.

Explicit non-goals: no AlembicAgent/AlembicPlugin/Alembic/AlembicDashboard edits; no real BiliDili/AlembicWorkspace data access or mutation; no query weighting/rank tuning, hardcoded query/Recipe ID/global synonyms, model replacement, Test work, Graph/Recipe Map changes, Plugin↔Alembic coupling, Git/host/role/knowledge-status gates, query-time maintenance or empty type-only contracts.

Implement the single combined AlembicAgent landing for the confirmed Recipe production/retrieval-quality demand, consuming accepted AlembicCore commit b711ea10aa5c67d1d75a58a18c0d56623e26c290 through its public contracts.

Required connected implementation:
1. Inventory the real Agent Recipe-producing call graph, including knowledge.submit, session-bound/opportunistic variants, and any cold-start or incremental producer path actually owned by Agent. Preserve non-Recipe behavior, but every Recipe submit must terminate at Core RecipeProductionPort with capability=knowledge-submit (or the exact other one of the four confirmed capabilities only where a real Agent caller owns it); do not call KnowledgeService.create or rebuild Core readiness/profile semantics locally.
2. Extend Agent producer schemas, prompts and deterministic front-loading so equivalent source evidence produces the Core RecipeRetrievalProfile semantics: project-primary summary, evidence-grounded technical English summary/concepts/scenarios/exclusions, stable provenance/source refs and source-content hash. English text is retrieval expression only; never use frozen queries, expected Recipe IDs, hardcoded/global synonyms, provider/rank output or invented facts.
3. Remove or replace unsafe mechanical coreCode repair. coreCode may be emitted only from a cited bounded code range matching the evidence; an invalid, unbounded, whole-file or unrelated-document range must leave coreCode empty or produce a stable Core readiness violation while the candidate remains pending/staging. Do not make provider/vector availability a submit or publish gate.
4. Surface Core readiness/profile violations in the existing Agent result/stop-loss evidence without parsing prose, preserve evidence ledger and session behavior, and keep pending/staging repairable truth. Do not add a second profile database/status machine or bypass publish readiness.
5. Keep changes confined to AlembicAgent; no Plugin/Alembic/Dashboard/Core edits, no real knowledge-root writes, no query ranking/Graph/Test work.

Required RED/GREEN and exit evidence:
- schema-to-runtime validation parity for every real Agent Recipe submit variant;
- equivalent evidence across cold/opportunistic/session-bound submit variants yields the same profile semantics where those variants exist;
- bounded range produces matching coreCode/provenance; whole-file, invalid and unrelated ranges cannot inject code and cannot activate;
- missing/ungrounded profile facts remain pending/staging with stable Core violation codes;
- provider offline does not change deterministic readiness or Agent submit result truth;
- real in-test Agent call reaches Core RecipeProductionPort and persists/profile-projects through the accepted contract; no empty adapter or disconnected type-only work;
- focused and full Agent tests, build/type/lint/import-boundary gates, git diff/check, two-stage self-review, clean single AlembicAgent commit with exact parent/commit and residual risks.

Implement the single combined AlembicPlugin landing for the confirmed Recipe production/retrieval-quality demand, starting from clean Plugin baseline 79f46cda0a1325b5e5a32a8e629fbb822ca65fdc and consuming accepted AlembicCore commit b711ea10aa5c67d1d75a58a18c0d56623e26c290 through public @alembic/core contracts. AlembicAgent commit cc85887c0cd88fd5d004c2d1f965eec0d8747caa is accepted behavioral evidence for field/code provenance and publish readiness, not an implementation dependency to import or copy.

Required connected implementation:
1. Inventory the real Codex host call graph for alembic_submit_knowledge, cold-start/bootstrap Recipe production, knowledge-rescan/incremental maintenance, lifecycle publish if Plugin owns one, and Search/Prime readers. Every Recipe-producing path actually owned by Plugin must terminate at Core RecipeProductionPort with the exact confirmed capability (knowledge-submit, cold-start, or incremental); do not call KnowledgeService.create, duplicate Agent internals, or introduce Alembic main-runtime coupling.
2. Extend real MCP schemas/results and host adapters so source evidence and Recipe fields can carry the Core RecipeRetrievalProfile wire contract and return structured production/readiness/profile diagnostics. Preserve Plugin stage-1/stage-2 host checks only for their legitimate content/evidence role; they must not redefine Core profile/readiness, infer English facts, parse prose errors, add provider/rank/Git/host/role/status gates, or block repairable pending/staging truth. Invalid, whole-file, documentation-as-code, or unrelated coreCode is empty/diagnosed through the shared contract while independently grounded profile facts survive.
3. Replace Plugin-owned fixed-region, duplicate sparse/dense, or generic Recipe-vector construction with Core RecipeRetrievalDocumentSet/projector output. Keyword and dense indexing must consume the same source/profile/document hashes and exact per-Recipe expected IDs. Raw paths, evidence IDs, quality bookkeeping and generation metadata remain metadata, not standalone retrieval candidates. Remove only replaced duplicate builders after proving all callers migrated.
4. Connect cold-start/rescan and any existing daemon/host maintenance path to Core generation planning/manifest/exact reconcile/shadow build/verified switch/rollback contracts. Full and incremental maintenance must derive byte-equivalent documents for the same Recipe; provider/model/dimension/projection/format changes create a new generation; deletion/deprecation cleanup works without provider. Maintenance remains explicit or lifecycle-owned outside request handlers.
5. Prove alembic_search_recipes and alembic_prime stay request-scoped read-only consumers of the accepted KnowledgeRetrievalPort/common retrieval truth. They must construct no writer, profile/projector persistence, reconcile, rebuild, generation switch, bootstrap, Git check, host-project gate, knowledge-status/visibility gate, or Alembic main-runtime dependency during a query. Existing no-knowledge behavior remains an ordinary empty/not-found result, not a precondition block.
6. Preserve Codex MCP annotations/output compatibility, skills/distribution/runtime boundaries and existing Graph/Recipe Map behavior. Confine changes to AlembicPlugin; no AlembicCore/AlembicAgent/Alembic/AlembicDashboard edits, vendor gitlink refresh, local plugin-cache refresh, real project knowledge-root mutation, Test work, query ranking/weight tuning, hardcoded queries/Recipe IDs/global synonyms, or new state machine.

Required RED/GREEN and exit evidence:
- real in-test MCP/host submit call reaches Core RecipeProductionPort, persists/profile-projects a native profile, returns stable readiness/profile/code-evidence fields, and never auto-publishes;
- field-only and exact documentation profile provenance survives independently from coreCode; whole-file/invalid/unrelated/documentation coreCode cannot inject code or activate;
- cold-start and incremental/rescan use the same Core production/projector contracts and yield identical document IDs/hashes for equal Recipe truth;
- Plugin legacy/fixed region builders and generic duplicate Recipe candidates have no remaining live caller; sparse/dense consume the same document-set/profile/source hashes;
- exact reconcile fixtures cover orphan/missing/partial/duplicate/hash/stale-generation cases through the Core maintenance surface; provider-offline delete/deprecate and failed shadow build preserve queryable active generation/rollback;
- Search and Prime request probes prove zero writes/zero maintenance invocation and preserve common truth/refill/raw-lane behavior;
- no direct Core source imports, Agent runtime reintroduction, Alembic main runtime import, disconnected type-only work, real data write, or query-specific tuning;
- run focused RED/GREEN tests, build:check/build, relevant unit/integration/e2e tests, npm run check, repo/Core/public/API/provider/boundary gates, Codex plugin smoke/verify/distribution/session checks appropriate to changed surfaces, git diff/check and two-stage self-review;
- one clean AlembicPlugin commit with exact parent/commit, changed files/symbols, raw command summaries, compatibility/deletion evidence and residual risks.
